§ `Functions`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation points at what it says` MEANS c's `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS c's `the target is`

-- Whether the text the citing words name is the text in force on a day. The only answer the sources held can give is the day it stopped being in force and the days from then on; for any earlier day,
-- and for a citation with no recorded end, the answer is NOTHING (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the named text is in force on` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the text the citing words name stopped being the text in force on`
        WHEN JUST stopped THEN IF day AT LEAST stopped THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the consolidation prints the named text as in force` MEANS NOT c's `the consolidation prints the named text as repealed`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the target holds the kind of proceeding the citing words name` MEANS c's `the target holds a proceeding of the kind the citing words name` EQUALS JUST TRUE

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs were read from the official instrument alone` MEANS
    c's `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    AND c's `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

GIVEN n IS A `A fee notice recital`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`years between the two indexes printed` MEANS n's `the year of the later index printed` - n's `the year of the earlier index printed`

GIVEN n IS A `A fee notice recital`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the earlier index is the one of the year before the later index` MEANS `years between the two indexes printed` n EQUALS 1

GIVEN t IS A `A printed title`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the title carries the old name` MEANS t's `the title carries` EQUALS `the words the 2019 rename replaced: ההגבלים העסקיים`

GIVEN t IS A `A printed title`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if the title carries the old name` MEANS IF `the title carries the old name` t THEN 1 ELSE 0

-- The four recorded titles of instruments under the Law (the Law's own title and the rename are not among them).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of recorded instruments under the Law whose title carries the old name` MEANS
    `one if the title carries the old name` (`title: the annual fee notice printed in KT 12149, p. 482`)
    + `one if the title carries the old name` (`title: the fee regulations of 1989`)
    + `one if the title carries the old name` (`title: the police-station order of 2000`)
    + `one if the title carries the old name` (`title: the 1964 regulations`)
